1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,528
Narrator: Scenario 68. Monitoring, performance, and reliability.

2
00:00:07,128 --> 00:00:16,992
B: The load test passed last week, yet production struggled during the sale. What did the test miss, and how can we trust the next result?

3
00:00:17,592 --> 00:00:27,072
A: The test represented request volume reasonably well, but not the production request mix, data size, or limits of the shared search dependency.

4
00:00:27,672 --> 00:00:38,448
C: We used mostly cached reads and a small catalog. During the sale, searches with multiple filters increased and reached the database more often.

5
00:00:39,048 --> 00:00:49,200
B: Could we simply double the test traffic and add application replicas? That seems faster than rebuilding the whole workload model before the next event.

6
00:00:49,800 --> 00:01:00,696
A: More replicas may increase pressure on the same dependency. We need to reproduce the actual bottleneck before deciding whether application capacity would help.

7
00:01:01,296 --> 00:01:13,080
C: I can build an anonymized workload from production proportions, with realistic catalog size, cold-cache periods, and the current search quota represented explicitly.

8
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:23,280
B: How long should it run? The previous test lasted twenty minutes, while the production slowdown appeared almost an hour into the campaign.

9
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:33,144
A: We need a longer steady-load phase to expose queue growth and resource accumulation, plus controlled bursts and a recovery period after traffic falls.

10
00:01:33,744 --> 00:01:46,848
C: I propose a two-hour steady phase. Pass criteria will cover completed searches, checkout success, tail latency, dependency saturation, and how quickly queues drain.

11
00:01:47,448 --> 00:01:58,320
B: Make the constraints visible in the report. A passing result should state the supported traffic profile, not imply unlimited readiness for any campaign.

12
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:10,416
A: We will agree on the workload and acceptance criteria Wednesday at 10:00 UTC. The test environment limits must also be documented before execution.

13
00:02:11,016 --> 00:02:22,152
C: I will prepare that proposal and identify production differences we cannot simulate. After the run, we will turn the measured bottlenecks into owned actions.
